  "term": "SCN",
  "definition": "SCN refers to solitary circumscribed neuroma, a noncancerous tumor of the peripheral nerve sheath made up of Schwann cells, axons, and perineurial fibroblasts. It usually develops in the skin of the head and neck or in the oral mucosa and typically appears as a single painless nodule.",
